The pipeline runs the following third-party programs, each in a Docker image
built from dependencies/<tool>/. This repository holds only their Dockerfiles:
each program is downloaded and built when its image is built, and its licence
files are copied into the image, under /usr/share/licenses/<program>/.

  - bcftools 1.24 (https://github.com/samtools/bcftools), under the MIT/Expat
    License
  - htslib 1.24 and 1.23 (https://github.com/samtools/htslib), built into
    bcftools and pbwt, under the MIT/Expat License, with some files under the
    Modified (3-clause) BSD License
  - pbwt v2.1 (https://github.com/richarddurbin/pbwt), Copyright (C) Genome
    Research Limited, under the Apache License 2.0, as stated in its source
    files
  - combine v0.8.0 (https://github.com/MRCIEU/combine-pbwt-sparsepaint), under
    the GNU General Public License, version 3; its third-party notices are in
    its NOTICE file
  - hcsvd v0.2.0 (https://github.com/MRCIEU/hc-svd), under the MIT License; its
    third-party notices are in its NOTICE file

The images are based on Debian and Alpine Linux, whose packages are distributed
under their own licences.

The test data in testdata/ is derived from the 1000 Genomes Project's
high-coverage phased genotypes (https://www.internationalgenome.org/).
